# Settings for smartclock-exporter.  See `smartclock-exporter --help`.
#
# Every line below is commented out and shows the built-in default.
# Uncomment one only to change it.

#SMARTCLOCK_EXPORTER_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:9979

# The daemons' sockets, one instance per subdirectory.  Every one is
# scraped, each sample labeled daemon="<instance>" and by the
# receiver's serial and model.  Set SMARTCLOCK_EXPORTER_DAEMON to list
# the daemons instead, comma-separated, each [NAME=]ENDPOINT: a socket
# or tcp://HOST:PORT.  The name is the daemon label.
#SMARTCLOCK_EXPORTER_RUN_DIR=/run/smartclockd

# The sensor service.
#SMARTCLOCK_EXPORTER_SENSORD=/run/smartclock-sensord/socket
